@@ -0,0 +1,147 @@
+# T-dense round 2 — working report
+
+Status: in progress. All calculations in this report are executed only on dirichlet through `DIRICHLET_IP=34.148.157.169 src/dirun.sh -c 2`. No commits, subagents, root research-note edits, or LaTeX manuscripts.
+
+## Scope and frontier
+
+**CONJECTURED (target, inherited).** For every real C >= 1 there exists c(C) > 0 such that every nonempty finite A of distinct positive integers with X=max A <= C|A| satisfies -min_x sum_{a in A}cos(ax) >= c(C)sqrt(|A|).
+
+**PROVED (quoted project inputs).** P38 gives this for its cumulative profile roundings; TD4 gives a sufficient third-moment criterion. P40 gives the spike-truncation criterion. None is a proof of the target for arbitrary C.
+
+**HEURISTIC (inherited).** P39-O(ii) proposes dense Bohr unions as an obstruction to every single denominator filter. The mixed triples and overlap/union errors require verification; finite growth cannot alone disprove its quantified LM statement.
+
+**New candidate mechanisms under investigation.** Exact finite Bohr-union audits; positive Fejer mixtures with independent Bernoulli thinning as a tractable infinite obstruction; reciprocal spike masks; local discrepancy expressed as shift variation rather than prefix mass alone.
+
+## Normalization correction discovered during setup
+
+**PROVED (new audit correction).** In P39's physical-space variance formula, the zero-frequency coefficient must be removed. For s=1_{A union(-A)}, g=2s-s(. -q)-s(. +q), and a_q=1_{q in A}, g(0)=-2a_q. Therefore the centered T=(1-cos(qx))f+a_q/2 has
+
+    V = (||g||_2^2 - 4a_q)/16,
+
+not the full norm divided by 16. Writing r(k)=sum_j s(j)s(j-k), this is
+
+    16V = 12n - 8r(q) + 2r(2q) - 4a_q.
+
+The quoted Delta and centered W formulas remain valid:
+
+    32W = Delta + 48a_q V + 4a_q,
+    Delta = 10c(0)-15c(q)+6c(2q)-c(3q).
+
+Proof: Fourier coefficients of H_q f are g/4; centering deletes g(0)/4. Expand the squared difference and then the centered cube. For A={1}, q=1, T=cos x-(1/2)cos 2x, giving V=5/8, whereas the uncentered norm gives 7/8. This correction does not change the previously verified TD4 coefficient formula or asymptotic obstruction.
+
+## Reproducibility
+
+Scratch directory: `.research/agents/tdense2_scratch/`. Exact finite claims and numerical minima will be recorded separately. Every claim below will be marked PROVED / NUMERICAL / HEURISTIC / CONJECTURED.
+
+## TD5: an effective infinite counterexample to LM-dense
+
+**PROVED (new paper proof; not kernel-checked).** There is a terminating algorithm producing, for every integer t >= 1024, a set A_t subset [1,X], X=2^t, with n>=X/16, such that, simultaneously for every integer 1<=q<=X,
+
+    V_q >= X/256,
+    W_q >= X^2/(2^28 J^2),       J=128(t+1).
+
+Consequently
+
+    W_q/V_q^(3/2) >= sqrt(X)/(2^30 J^2) -> infinity
+
+uniformly in q. Moreover the algorithm can require f_A(pi)<=-sqrt(X)/128, so M(A)>=sqrt(n)/128. This disproves LM-dense as quantified in P39, already at C=16. It does not disprove T-dense. The construction below is a positive Fejer-mixture analogue of the proposed Bohr unions, rather than a proof of the sharp-cutoff union heuristic.
+
+### TD5.1. Positive signal and effective choices of angles
+
+**PROVED.** Write N=X+1 and
+
+    F_N(x) = (1/N)|sum_{j=0}^{N-1} exp(ijx)|^2,
+    B(x) = F_N(x)+(1/(4J))sum_{i=1}^J [F_N(x-theta_i)+F_N(x+theta_i)].
+
+All integrals use normalized Haar measure on the circle. Thus B>=0, integral B=3/2, integral B^2<=(9/4)N (convexity/Jensen applied to its positive mixture), and
+
+    F(x):=(B(x)-3/2)/4 = sum_{m=1}^X p_m cos(mx),
+    p_m=(1/2)(1-m/N)[1+(1/(2J))sum_i cos(m theta_i)].
+
+In particular, w_m/4 <= p_m <= 3w_m/4 <=3/4, where w_m=1-m/N.
+
+Take theta_i independently uniform on the P=16X equally spaced points. For each 1<=q<=X the order of q in Z/PZ is at least 16 and is a power of two, so P(cos(q theta_i)<=0)>=1/2. The elementary binomial Chernoff bound gives
+
+    P(#{i:cos(q theta_i)<=0}<J/4) <= exp(-J/8).
+
+For completeness, Markov applied to exp(-log(3)*K) bounds this by
+`[3^(1/4)*(2/3)]^J <= exp(-J/8)`; increasing each success probability can only improve the bound. Union over q costs at most X exp(-J/8). Since P>X, discrete Fourier orthogonality gives E B(pi)=F_N(pi)+1/2<=1. Markov therefore bounds P(B(pi)>16) by 1/16. Their sum is less than 1. Choose the lexicographically first angle tuple satisfying
+
+    #{i:cos(q theta_i)<=0}>=J/4 for every q<=X, and B(pi)<=16.
+
+This is an effective finite selection: all values are real algebraic numbers in cyclotomic fields, so each comparison is decidable exactly. Repeated angles are allowed and do not invalidate any positive-mixture inequality.
+
+### TD5.2. A cubic lower bound for every filter, with no mixed-triple estimate
+
+**PROVED.** On |u|<=1/(4N), the sine formula gives F_N(u)>=N/4. If cos(q theta_i)<=0, then q<N and
+
+    1-cos(q(theta_i+u)) >= 3/4 >=1/2.
+
+Thus, for H_q=1-cos(qx), integrating over that interval,
+
+    integral H_q^3 F_N(x-theta_i)^3 >= N^2/8192.
+
+Indeed its normalized length is 1/(4 pi N), and the crude lower bound is N^2/(2048 pi)>N^2/8192. Since every summand of B is nonnegative, its cube dominates the sum of the cubes of its summands, even if bumps overlap. At least J/4 of the chosen positive shifts contribute, giving
+
+    integral H_q^3 B^3 >= N^2/(2^21 J^2).
+
+Expanding (B-3/2)^3/64, dropping its positive linear term, using H_q^3<=8 and integral B^2<=(9/4)N, gives
+
+    integral (H_q F)^3 >= N^2/(2^27 J^2)-2N.
+
+Let T_0=H_q F+p_q/2. Since mean(H_q F)=-p_q/2 and p_q>=0, the centered third moment equals the raw third moment plus `(3p_q/2) Var(H_q F)+p_q^3/8`, which is nonnegative. Also integral T_0^2<=N. Hence
+
+    integral T_0^3 >= N^2/(2^27 J^2)-2N.
+
+This is the point that replaces the unproved mixed-triple step in P39-O(ii).
+
+### TD5.3. Rounding errors and density
+
+**PROVED.** Independently select a_m in {0,1} with probability p_m. Put xi_m=a_m-p_m and Z=sum xi_m cos(mx). Then
+
+    sum p_m >= X/8,
+    sigma^2:=sum p_m(1-p_m)>=X/32.
+
+The second inequality uses 1-p_m>=1/4 and sum w_m=X/2. Hoeffding gives P(n<X/16)<=exp(-X/128).
+
+Use a grid of K=64X^2 points on the circle and set R=10 ceil(sqrt(X(t+1))). Since |Z'|<=X(X+1)/2<=X^2, its value differs from that at a nearest grid point by less than 1. At a fixed point the independent summands have mean zero and absolute value <=1, so the (weaker than usual) Hoeffding bound `P(|Z|>u)<=2 exp(-u^2/(2X))` suffices. A union bound shows
+
+    P(||Z||_infinity>R) <= 128X^2 exp(-(R-1)^2/(2X)),
+
+which is less than 1/512 for t>=1024. No sampled numerical minimum is used in this proof.
+
+The centered noise in T_q is E_q=H_q Z+xi_q/2, so ||E_q||_infinity<=3R. Since integral T_0^2<=N and R>=sqrt(N), expansion and Cauchy give
+
+    |integral (T_0+E_q)^3-integral T_0^3|
+        <=9RN+27R^2 sqrt(N)+27R^3 <=63R^3.
+
+For all q this proves W_q>=N^2/(2^27 J^2)-2N-63R^3. For t>=1024,
+
+    R<=20 sqrt(X(t+1)), J=128(t+1),
+    2N+63R^3 <= X^2/(2^28 J^2).
+
+One sufficient elementary inequality is `2^(t/2)>=2^64(t+1)^4`. It holds at t=1024 because the right side is less than 2^108 and the left side is 2^512, and the ratio increases thereafter: its consecutive ratio is sqrt(2)*((t+1)/(t+2))^4>1. This proves the stated W bound.
+
+**PROVED.** Uniform positive variance can also be imposed. The coefficient of xi_m in centered T_q is H_q cos(mx)+(1/2)1_{m=q}; its squared integral is at least 1/4 (the exceptional q=2m gives exactly 1/4). Independence yields E V_q>=sigma^2/4>=X/128. Changing one a_m changes at most six entries of g_q, each in [-2,2], so |change in V_q|<=24/16<2. McDiarmid's elementary bounded-differences bound gives
+
+    P(V_q<X/256)<=exp(-X/131072).
+
+Union over q is less than 1/512 for t>=1024. This supplies the nonvacuous V bound; the divergence conclusion itself only needs the cubic bound and V_q<=2n, the latter following from H_q<=2 and integral f^2=n/2.
+
+### TD5.4. A separate square-root negative witness
+
+**PROVED.** At pi, the chosen signal satisfies F(pi)<4. The independent centered sum Z(pi)=sum (-1)^m xi_m has variance sigma^2>=X/32 and fourth moment at most 3sigma^4+sigma^2<=4sigma^4. Holder interpolation gives E|Z(pi)|>=sigma/2. Since E Z(pi)=0, E Z(pi)_- >=sigma/4. Paley-Zygmund applied to its negative part now gives
+
+    P(Z(pi)<=-sigma/8)>=1/64.
+
+In detail, P(Y>=(1/2)EY)>=(EY)^2/(4 EY^2), with EY>=sigma/4 and EY^2<=sigma^2. The preceding density, variance and uniform-error failure probabilities total less than 1/128 (the much smaller density term is included). Their complement therefore intersects this negative-tail event. For t>=1024, sigma/8-4>=sqrt(X)/128. The intersection yields f_A(pi)<=-sqrt(X)/128.
+
+### TD5.5. A terminating integer-only output algorithm
+
+**PROVED.** For input t>=1024, set X=2^t and J=128(t+1). Enumerate subsets A of [1,X] lexicographically until all of the following exact tests hold:
+
+1. n>=X/16;
+2. for every q<=X, the rational moments (computed by finite integer convolution) satisfy V_q>=X/256 and W_q>=X^2/(2^28 J^2);
+3. the integer sum sum_{a in A}(-1)^a is <=-sqrt(X)/128 (decide using integer signs and squares).
+
+The probabilistic proof above proves that the search terminates for every such t. It is an effective explicit family, with deliberately enormous computational complexity and threshold; it is not offered as a practical construction at t=1024. The proof uses random positive Fejer mixtures to establish existence of a passing subset, but the final selection tests do not require algebraic probabilities or numerical trigonometry. No claim is made that this is the original sharp Bohr-union family or that its constants are optimized.
diff --git a/.research/agents/tdense2_scratch/audit.py b/.research/agents/tdense2_scratch/audit.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9fb09f0935af34ab79788cf3dd6d9399f2af3c2a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.research/agents/tdense2_scratch/audit.py
@@ -0,0 +1,292 @@
+"""Round-2 finite audits. EXECUTE ONLY with src/dirun.sh -c 2.
+
+Exact modular FLINT polynomial products, two-prime CRT, proved count bound.
+The numerical cosine minima and eigenvector search are explicitly numerical;
+the rounded rational moment witnesses are evaluated in exact arithmetic.
+"""
+import argparse
+import hashlib
+import json
+import math
+import platform
+import sys
+import time
+from fractions import Fraction as F
+from pathlib import Path
+
+import numpy as np
+from flint import fmpz_poly, nmod_poly
+from scipy.linalg import eigh
+
+sys.path.insert(0, "src")
+from box_minlam import true_min
+
+OUT = Path('.research/agents/tdense2_scratch')
+PRIMES = (998244353, 1004535809)
+P_ALPHA = 2147483647
+
+
+def exact_counts(A, save=None):
+    X, n = max(A), len(A)
+    coeff = [0] * (2*X+1)
+    for a in A:
+        coeff[X-a] = coeff[X+a] = 1
+    bound = (2*n)**2
+    assert bound < PRIMES[0]*PRIMES[1]
+    residues, pairs = [], []
+    for p in PRIMES:
+        f = nmod_poly(coeff, p)
+        f2 = f*f
+        f3 = f2*f
+        residues.append(np.array([int(f3[3*X+k]) for k in range(3*X+1)], dtype=np.int64))
+        # Pair counts <=2n, hence the first prime alone is sufficient here.
+        if not pairs:
+            pairs.append(np.array([int(f2[2*X+k]) for k in range(2*X+1)], dtype=np.int64))
+    p, r = PRIMES
+    c = residues[0] + p * (((residues[1]-residues[0])*pow(p, -1, r)) % r)
+    assert int(c.max()) <= bound
+    assert int(c[0]) % 6 == 0
+    if save:
+        np.savez_compressed(save, c=c, r=pairs[0])
+    return c, pairs[0]
+
+
+def best_filter(A, save=None, qmax=None):
+    X, n = max(A), len(A)
+    c, r = exact_counts(A, save)
+    aa = np.zeros(X+1, dtype=np.int64)
+    aa[A] = 1
+    qmax = X if qmax is None else qmax
+    if qmax>X:
+        aa=np.pad(aa,(0,qmax-X))
+        c=np.pad(c,(0,3*(qmax-X)))
+        r=np.pad(r,(0,2*(qmax-X)))
+    qs = np.arange(1, qmax+1)
+    aq = aa[qs]
+    v = 12*n - 8*r[qs] + 2*r[2*qs] - 4*aq
+    delta = 10*c[0] - 15*c[qs] + 6*c[2*qs] - c[3*qs]
+    w = delta + 3*aq*v + 4*aq
+    admissible = np.flatnonzero(5*v >= 8*n)
+    assert len(admissible)
+    best = None
+    # Compare signs and squares by Python integers: exact minimizer of W/V^(3/2).
+    for i in admissible:
+        vi, wi = int(v[i]), int(w[i])
+        if best is None:
+            best = int(i)
+            continue
+        vb, wb = int(v[best]), int(w[best])
+        si, sb = (wi>0)-(wi<0), (wb>0)-(wb<0)
+        if si < sb or (si == sb and si and
+                si*(wi*wi*vb**3 - wb*wb*vi**3) < 0):
+            best = int(i)
+    q, vi, wi = best+1, int(v[best]), int(w[best])
+    ratio = 2*wi/vi**1.5
+    lbm = (math.sqrt(ratio*ratio+4)-ratio)/2 * math.sqrt(vi/16)
+    result = dict(q=q, V=str(F(vi,16)), W=str(F(wi,32)),
+        V_over_n=vi/(16*n), min_W_over_V_threehalves=ratio,
+        admissible_count=len(admissible), all_q_checked=qmax,
+        exact_argmin=True, cmax=int(c.max()), c0=int(c[0]),
+        c_at_0_q_2q_3q=[int(c[k*q]) for k in range(4)],
+        third_moment_M_lb_numerical=(lbm+int(aa[q])/2)/2,
+        min_V_over_n=float(v.min())/(16*n))
+    return result
+
+
+def bohr(X, seed, profile='quadratic', factor=8):
+    J = math.ceil(factor*math.log(X)/math.log(math.log(X)))
+    # epsilon=1/(8J) exactly. C0=2 in the brief's epsilon=1/(4 C0 J).
+    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)
+    mm = np.arange(1, X+1, dtype=np.int64)
+    chosen = None
+    for trial in range(100):
+        numerators = rng.choice(P_ALPHA-1, size=J, replace=False)+1
+        union = np.zeros(X, dtype=bool)
+        active = np.zeros(X, dtype=np.int16)
+        for a in numerators:
+            rr = (mm*a) % P_ALPHA
+            dd = np.minimum(rr, P_ALPHA-rr)
+            union |= (dd*(8*J) < P_ALPHA)
+            yes = np.zeros(X, dtype=bool)
+            for k in (1,2,3):
+                rk = (rr*k) % P_ALPHA
+                dk = np.minimum(rk, P_ALPHA-rk)
+                yes |= (dk*(8*J) < 3*P_ALPHA)
+            active += yes
+        if int(active.max()) <= J//2:
+            chosen = (numerators, union, active, trial)
+            break
+    if chosen is None:
+        raise RuntimeError('No alpha sample passed the stated finite activity condition')
+    numerators, union, active, trial = chosen
+    # Rational thinning probabilities, exact integer Bernoulli realization.
+    den = 5*(X+1)**2
+    if profile == 'quadratic':
+        threshold = 4*(X+1-mm)**2
+    elif profile == 'flat':
+        threshold = np.full(X, 4*(X+1)**2, dtype=np.int64)
+    else:
+        raise ValueError(profile)
+    keep = rng.integers(0, den, size=X, dtype=np.int64) < threshold
+    A = mm[union & keep].astype(int).tolist()
+    return A, dict(kind='Bohr union', X_ambient=X, seed=seed, J=J,
+        epsilon=f'1/{8*J}', C0=2, alpha_denominator=P_ALPHA,
+        alpha_numerators=numerators.astype(int).tolist(), alpha_trials=trial+1,
+        maximum_active=int(active.max()), activity_limit=J//2,
+        union_size=int(union.sum()), thinning=f'(4/5)*(1-m/{X+1})^2' if profile=='quadratic' else '4/5',
+        exact_membership_and_thinning=True)
+
+
+def fejer(X, seed, jfactor=2):
+    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)
+    J = math.ceil(jfactor*math.log(X))
+    nums = rng.choice(P_ALPHA-1, size=J, replace=False)+1
+    mm = np.arange(1, X+1, dtype=np.int64)
+    modulation = np.zeros(X)
+    negative_count = np.zeros(X, dtype=np.int16)
+    for a in nums:
+        theta = 2*math.pi*((mm*a)%P_ALPHA)/P_ALPHA
+        cc = np.cos(theta)
+        modulation += cc
+        negative_count += cc <= 0
+    prob = .5*(1-mm/(X+1))*(1+.5/J*modulation)
+    A = mm[rng.random(X) < prob].astype(int).tolist()
+    return A, dict(kind='positive Fejer mixture Bernoulli', X_ambient=X,
+        seed=seed, J=J, delta=.5, modulation_amplitude=.5,
+        alpha_denominator=P_ALPHA, alpha_numerators=nums.astype(int).tolist(),
+        minimum_negative_cos_count=int(negative_count.min()),
+        probability_evaluation='floating point (saved realization is an exact integer set)')
+
+
+def moments(A, q, order=7):
+    X=max(A)
+    D=X+q
+    a=set(A)
+    g=[]
+    for j in range(-D,D+1):
+        if j==0:
+            g.append(0)
+        else:
+            av=lambda k: int(abs(k) in a)
+            g.append(2*av(j)-av(j-q)-av(j+q) if q else 2*av(j))
+    poly=fmpz_poly(g)
+    cur=fmpz_poly([1])
+    out=[F(1)]
+    for k in range(1,order+1):
+        cur=cur*poly
+        out.append(F(int(cur[k*D]),4**k))
+    return out
+
+
+def moment_witness(A, q, order=7):
+    mus=moments(A,q,order)
+    scale=max(1, round(math.sqrt(len(A))))
+    vals=[float(m/scale**k) for k,m in enumerate(mus)]
+    out=[]
+    for d in range(1,(order+1)//2):
+        h0=np.array([[vals[i+j] for j in range(d+1)] for i in range(d+1)])
+        h1=np.array([[vals[i+j+1] for j in range(d+1)] for i in range(d+1)])
+        ev,evec=eigh(h1,h0)
+        vec=evec[:,0]
+        vec=vec/max(abs(vec))
+        pp=[int(round(float(t)*10**9)) for t in vec]
+        den=sum(F(pp[i]*pp[j],scale**(i+j))*mus[i+j]
+                for i in range(d+1) for j in range(d+1))
+        num=sum(F(pp[i]*pp[j],scale**(i+j))*mus[i+j+1]
+                for i in range(d+1) for j in range(d+1))
+        assert den>0
+        lb=-num/den
+        Mlb=(lb+F(int(q in A),2))/2 if q else lb
+        out.append(dict(degree=d, highest_moment=2*d+1, scale=scale,
+            integer_polynomial_coefficients=pp,
+            exact_m_lower_bound=str(lb), exact_M_lower_bound=str(Mlb),
+            M_lower_bound=float(Mlb), M_lb_over_sqrt_n=float(Mlb)/math.sqrt(len(A)),
+            eigenvalue_numerical=float(ev[0])))
+    return dict(q=q, moments=[str(m) for m in mus], witnesses=out)
+
+
+def run_one(name,A,params=None,with_moments=False):
+    A=sorted(set(map(int,A)))
+    t=time.time()
+    safe=name.replace('/','_').replace(':','_')
+    row=dict(name=name,n=len(A),X=max(A),C=max(A)/len(A),A=A,parameters=params)
+    row['filter']=best_filter(A,OUT/(safe+'_counts.npz'),
+        qmax=params.get('X_ambient') if params else None)
+    (fm,xm), _, G=true_min(A,over=64)
+    direct=float(np.cos(np.array(A)*xm).sum())
+    row['minimum_numerical']=dict(M=-float(fm),x=float(xm),R=-float(fm)/math.sqrt(len(A)),
+        grid_half_count=G,fft_direct_disagreement=direct-float(fm),certified=False)
+    if with_moments:
+        row['higher_moments']=[moment_witness(A,q) for q in (0,row['filter']['q'])]
+    row['seconds']=time.time()-t
+    (OUT/(safe+'.json')).write_text(json.dumps(row,indent=2))
+    summary={k:v for k,v in row.items() if k not in ('A','higher_moments','parameters')}
+    if params:
+        summary['parameters']={k:v for k,v in params.items() if k not in ('alpha_numerators',)}
+    if with_moments:
+        summary['moment_M_bounds']=[dict(q=m['q'],bounds=[w['M_lb_over_sqrt_n'] for w in m['witnesses']]) for m in row['higher_moments']]
+    print(json.dumps(summary),flush=True)
+    return summary
+
+
+def selftest():
+    from collections import Counter
+    rng=np.random.default_rng(712)
+    for X in range(1,22):
+        for _ in range(3):
+            A=[int(a) for a in range(1,X+1) if rng.random()<.6] or [X]
+            c,r=exact_counts(A)
+            S=A+[-a for a in A]
+            rr=Counter(a+b for a in S for b in S)
+            cc=Counter(a+b+c for a in S for b in S for c in S)
+            assert all(int(v)==cc[k] for k,v in enumerate(c))
+            assert all(int(v)==rr[k] for k,v in enumerate(r))
+            for q in range(1,max(A)+1):
+                mu=moments(A,q,3)
+                aq=int(q in A)
+                def rv(k): return int(r[k]) if k<len(r) else 0
+                def cv(k): return int(c[k]) if k<len(c) else 0
+                v=12*len(A)-8*rv(q)+2*rv(2*q)-4*aq
+                w=10*cv(0)-15*cv(q)+6*cv(2*q)-cv(3*q)+3*aq*v+4*aq
+                assert mu[1]==0 and mu[2]==F(v,16) and mu[3]==F(w,32)
+    print(json.dumps(dict(selftest='PASS',exact_sets=63,python=platform.python_version())),flush=True)
+
+
+def main():
+    parser=argparse.ArgumentParser()
+    parser.add_argument('--mode',choices=['selftest','family','benchmarks','moments'],required=True)
+    parser.add_argument('--sizes',type=int,nargs='*',default=[4096,16384,65536,200000])
+    parser.add_argument('--kinds',nargs='*',default=['bohr','fejer'])
+    parser.add_argument('--moments',action='store_true')
+    args=parser.parse_args()
+    OUT.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
+    if args.mode=='selftest':
+        return selftest()
+    summaries=[]
+    if args.mode=='family':
+        for kind in args.kinds:
+            for X in args.sizes:
+                seed=2026101900+X
+                A,params=(bohr(X,seed) if kind=='bohr' else fejer(X,seed))
+                summaries.append(run_one(f'{kind}_X{X}',A,params,args.moments))
+    elif args.mode=='benchmarks':
+        rows=json.load(open('.research/agents/tdense_scratch/probe.json'))['records']
+        for row in rows:
+            summaries.append(run_one('benchmark_'+row['name'],row['A'],with_moments=args.moments))
+        for name,A in [('interval_512',list(range(1,513))),
+            ('dilated_intervals_512',sorted(set(list(range(2,1025,2))+list(range(3,1537,3)))) )]:
+            summaries.append(run_one(name,A,with_moments=args.moments))
+    elif args.mode=='moments':
+        for kind in args.kinds:
+            for X in args.sizes:
+                path=OUT/f'{kind}_X{X}.json'
+                row=json.load(open(path))
+                row['higher_moments']=[moment_witness(row['A'],q) for q in (0,row['filter']['q'])]
+                path.write_text(json.dumps(row,indent=2))
+                print(json.dumps(dict(name=row['name'],bounds=[dict(q=m['q'],M_lb_over_sqrt_n=[w['M_lb_over_sqrt_n'] for w in m['witnesses']]) for m in row['higher_moments']])),flush=True)
+        return
+    (OUT/(args.mode+'_summary.json')).write_text(json.dumps(summaries,indent=2))
+
+
+if __name__=='__main__':
+    main()
diff --git a/.research/agents/tdense2_scratch/extra.py b/.research/agents/tdense2_scratch/extra.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ca192ff69d712cd654bb4230068208d450b32871
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.research/agents/tdense2_scratch/extra.py
@@ -0,0 +1,130 @@
+"""Only execute on the VM through dirun.sh -c 2. Additional targeted probes."""
+import json
+import math
+import sys
+from pathlib import Path
+import numpy as np
+
+sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).parent))
+from audit import OUT, P_ALPHA, bohr, run_one, moment_witness
+
+
+def mean_half(v):
+    return float((v.sum()-(v[0]+v[-1])/2)/(len(v)-1))
+
+
+def mask_probe(kind,X,over):
+    row=json.load(open(OUT/f'{kind}_X{X}.json'))
+    par=row['parameters']
+    mm=np.arange(1,X+1,dtype=np.int64)
+    if kind=='bohr':
+        union=np.zeros(X,dtype=bool)
+        for a in par['alpha_numerators']:
+            rr=(mm*a)%P_ALPHA
+            union |= np.minimum(rr,P_ALPHA-rr)*(8*par['J'])<P_ALPHA
+        prob=.8*(1-mm/(X+1))**2*union
+    else:
+        cc=np.zeros(X)
+        for a in par['alpha_numerators']:
+            cc+=np.cos(2*math.pi*((mm*a)%P_ALPHA)/P_ALPHA)
+        prob=.5*(1-mm/(X+1))*(1+.5/par['J']*cc)
+    G=1<<math.ceil(math.log2(over*X))
+    coef=np.zeros(G)
+    coef[row['A']]=1
+    f=np.fft.rfft(coef).real
+    coef[:]=0
+    coef[1:X+1]=prob
+    signal=np.fft.rfft(coef).real
+    out=[]
+    for name,H in [('reciprocal_abs_expected_signal',1/(1+abs(signal))),
+                   ('positive_spike_clip',np.minimum(1,math.sqrt(row['n'])/np.maximum(f,1e-100)))]:
+        Y=H*f
+        mu=mean_half(Y)
+        T=Y-mu
+        V=mean_half(T*T)
+        W=mean_half(T*T*T)
+        b=W/V**1.5
+        m=2*math.sqrt(V)/(math.sqrt(b*b+4)+b)
+        out.append(dict(mask=name,mu=mu,V_over_n=V/row['n'],
+            W_over_V_threehalves=b,M_lb_over_sqrt_n=(m-mu)/math.sqrt(row['n']),
+            H_mean=mean_half(H)))
+    return dict(kind=kind,X_ambient=X,grid_full_size=G,status='NUMERICAL quadrature, not certified',masks=out)
+
+
+def local_rounding(X,B=4096,front=.05):
+    # Exact counts at block boundaries, arbitrary rearrangement inside each block.
+    den=2*X*X
+    acc=old=0
+    aa=np.zeros(X+1,dtype=np.int64)
+    for start in range(1,X+1,B):
+        end=min(X,start+B-1)
+        for j in range(start,end+1):
+            acc+=(X-j)**2
+        new=acc//den
+        count=new-old
+        old=new
+        if start<=front*X:
+            # 1100 blocks give high q=2 variation.
+            positions=[start+4*(k//2)+(k%2) for k in range(count)]
+        else:
+            # A single q=2 chain gives small q=2 variation.
+            positions=[start+2*k for k in range(count)]
+        assert all(p<=end for p in positions)
+        aa[positions]=1
+    p=np.r_[0,.5*(1-np.arange(1,X+1)/X)**2]
+    discrepancy=float(abs(np.cumsum(aa-p)).max())
+    results=[]
+    for q in [2,4,8,16]:
+        D=X+q
+        ext=np.pad(aa,(0,q))
+        j=np.arange(1,D+1)
+        b=ext[j]-(ext[abs(j-q)]+np.where(j+q<=D,ext[np.minimum(j+q,D)],0))/2
+        e=b*b
+        E=float(e.sum())
+        ws=np.arange(1,D+1)
+        p0=np.cumsum(e)
+        p1=np.cumsum(e*ws)
+        p2=np.cumsum(e*ws*ws)
+        S=p0-2*p1/(ws+1)+p2/(ws+1)**2
+        W=2*(ws+1)/3+1/(3*(ws+1))
+        C=.811*(D+ws+1)+71/300
+        lbs=(W*E-C*S)/(2*(C-W))
+        i=int(lbs.argmax())
+        results.append(dict(q=q,E=E,E_over_X=E/X,best_w=i+1,
+            best_m_square=float(lbs[i]),best_m_square_over_X=float(lbs[i])/X))
+    return dict(X=X,B=B,front=front,n=int(aa.sum()),max_A=int(np.flatnonzero(aa)[-1]),
+        prefix_discrepancy=discrepancy,prefix_discrepancy_bound=B+1,results=results)
+
+
+if __name__=='__main__':
+    mode=sys.argv[1]
+    if mode=='bohr4':
+        res=[]
+        for X in [4096,16384,65536,200000]:
+            A,par=bohr(X,2026101900+X,factor=4)
+            res.append(run_one(f'bohr4_X{X}',A,par,with_moments=True))
+        (OUT/'bohr4_summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(res,indent=2))
+    elif mode=='masks':
+        res=[]
+        for kind in ['bohr','fejer']:
+            for X in [4096,16384,65536,200000]:
+                for over in [16,32]:
+                    row=mask_probe(kind,X,over)
+                    res.append(row)
+                    print(json.dumps(row),flush=True)
+        (OUT/'masks.json').write_text(json.dumps(res,indent=2))
+    elif mode=='local':
+        res=[]
+        for X in [65536,262144,1048576]:
+            row=local_rounding(X)
+            res.append(row)
+            print(json.dumps(row),flush=True)
+        (OUT/'local.json').write_text(json.dumps(res,indent=2))
+    elif mode=='moments':
+        for kind in ['bohr','fejer']:
+            for X in [4096,16384,65536,200000]:
+                path=OUT/f'{kind}_X{X}.json'
+                row=json.load(open(path))
+                row['higher_moments']=[moment_witness(row['A'],q) for q in [0,row['filter']['q']]]
+                path.write_text(json.dumps(row,indent=2))
+                print(json.dumps(dict(name=row['name'],bounds=[dict(q=m['q'],M_lb_over_sqrt_n=[w['M_lb_over_sqrt_n'] for w in m['witnesses']]) for m in row['higher_moments']])),flush=True)

