codex
I have a paper proof that LM-dense fails for an effective infinite family of dense sets, using positive Fejér mixtures followed by Bernoulli thinning. The construction also has a separate proved \(\sqrt n\) negative witness. Its threshold and running time are enormous, and it does not prove the original sharp Bohr-union heuristic.

On the computable Bohr examples, fifth and seventh moments improve the certificate substantially. I’m now testing spike masks and finishing the local-discrepancy result: bounded prefix discrepancy permits rearrangements that create large filter energy at the front.

